The sprite extraction and row-generation pipeline under `src/lib/sprite/` is a
TypeScript port of sprite-gen's Python implementation. No Python runtime is
bundled; the algorithms, constants, and pipeline structure were ported. The
files below carry the port, each naming its upstream source in its header:

    src/lib/sprite/request.ts        <- sprite_gen/prepare.py
                                        (normalize_cell, normalize_states,
                                         DEFAULT_STATES, state grading,
                                         state_motion_phases membership)
    src/lib/sprite/chroma-key.ts     <- sprite_gen/prepare.py
                                        (subject sampling, candidate scoring)
    src/lib/sprite/layout-guide.ts   <- sprite_gen/prepare.py (draw_guide)
    src/lib/sprite/row-prompt.ts     <- sprite_gen/prepare.py (row_prompt,
                                        STYLE_DEFAULT, STATE_REQUIREMENTS,
                                        TRANSPARENCY_ARTIFACT_RULES, anchor lock)
    src/lib/sprite/directions.ts     <- sprite_gen/prepare.py (directions block)
    src/lib/sprite/generation-plan.ts<- sprite_gen/prepare.py
                                        (build_generation_plan)
    src/lib/sprite/base-gate.ts      <- sprite_gen/prepare.py
                                        (detect_reference_background)
    src/lib/sprite/anchor.ts         <- sprite_gen/anchor.py
    src/lib/sprite/anchor-image.ts   <- sprite_gen/anchor.py (anchor_image)
    src/lib/sprite/chroma-clean.ts   <- sprite_gen/extract.py
                                        (remove_chroma_background)
    src/lib/sprite/chroma-ycbcr.ts   <- sprite_gen/extract.py
                                        (remove_chroma_background_ycbcr and its
                                         helpers: rgb_to_ycc, smoothstep,
                                         detect_background_key_ycc, _matte_ycc,
                                         _flood_clear_background_ycc,
                                         key_residue_fraction_ycc,
                                         _cleanup_alpha_ycc)
    src/lib/sprite/extract.ts        <- sprite_gen/extract.py
                                        (connected components, fit_to_cell,
                                         extract_slot_frames)
    src/lib/sprite/atlas.ts          <- sprite_gen/compose_atlas.py
    src/lib/sprite/preview.ts        <- sprite_gen/preview.py
    src/lib/sprite/gif.ts            <- sprite_gen/gif_utils.py
    src/lib/image-backend/codex-rollout.ts
                                     <- sprite_gen/gen/codex_provider.py

The following notices are inherited from sprite-gen's own NOTICE, for the parts
of it that this port carries.

--- inherited from sprite-gen ---

sprite-gen is inspired by the Apache-2.0 licensed hatch-pet component-row
workflow. It targets generic game sprite atlases and does not include Codex pet
assets, pet packages, or hatch-pet visual assets.

The alpha-weighted mass-centroid frame alignment (`_alpha_centroid_x` in
sprite_gen/extract.py, ported here as `alphaCentroidX` in
`src/lib/sprite/extract.ts`) is a port of the alignment from
perfectpixel-studio (https://github.com/gykim80/perfectpixel-studio,
internal/sprite/extract.go), Copyright Andrew Kim (gykim80), MIT License.
This port uses it only in sprite-gen's own default `foot-centroid` mode; the
`align_x: "alpha-centroid"` mode itself is not ported.

The opt-in `chroma.mode: "ycbcr"` background matting (sprite_gen/extract.py,
ported here as `src/lib/sprite/chroma-ycbcr.ts`) is a port of the
chrominance-plane matting — CbCr border-mode key detection, Hermite soft matte,
key-direction despill, border flood fill and the pure-key rematte
self-diagnostic — from perfectpixel-studio
(https://github.com/gykim80/perfectpixel-studio, internal/sprite/chroma.go),
Copyright Andrew Kim (gykim80), MIT License.

`sprite_gen/gen/codex_provider.py`, from which
`src/lib/image-backend/codex-rollout.ts` derives its rollout parsing and output
recovery, is itself a port of the standalone `image-gen` skill
(MIT, aldegad/image-gen).

--- not ported ---

These perfectpixel-studio derived parts of sprite-gen are NOT ported here, so
their notices do not apply to this repository: `segmentation: "projection"`
(sprite_gen/segment.py) and the `estimate_pixel_grid_runlen` pitch estimator.
If either is ported later, the corresponding notice from sprite-gen's NOTICE
must be added above.
